# Zybo Z7-10 user-I/O pin reference
#
# Board:  Digilent Zybo Z7-10 (Rev. B)
# Device: xc7z010clg400-1 (Zynq-7000 SoC)
# I/O standard for every pin below: LVCMOS33
#
# PROVENANCE
# ----------
# Transcribed from Digilent's official master constraint file, which covers
# both the Zybo Z7-10 and the Z7-20 (they share a board layout and differ only
# in the PL device fitted):
#
#   https://github.com/Digilent/digilent-xdc/blob/master/Zybo-Z7-Master.xdc
#
# scripts/check_pins.py diffs syn/vivado/zybo_z7_10.xdc against this file, so a
# typo in a pin or an I/O standard is a build failure rather than a board that
# quietly does nothing. Signals this design does not drive are listed for
# completeness, so that a misspelled port name is reported as unknown rather
# than silently accepted.
#
# NAMING
# ------
# Digilent names the switches sw[0]..sw[3]. This design uses a single switch and
# declares it as a scalar port `sw0`, so that name is listed alongside the board
# name for the same physical pin. Both are correct; only `sw0` is assigned.
#
# format: <signal> <pin> <iostandard>

# 125 MHz PL oscillator
sysclk K17 LVCMOS33

# Slide switches
sw[0] G15 LVCMOS33
sw0 G15 LVCMOS33
sw[1] P15 LVCMOS33
sw[2] W13 LVCMOS33
sw[3] T16 LVCMOS33

# Pushbuttons (read high when pressed)
btn[0] K18 LVCMOS33
btn[1] P16 LVCMOS33
btn[2] K19 LVCMOS33
btn[3] Y16 LVCMOS33

# User LEDs LD0-LD3
led[0] M14 LVCMOS33
led[1] M15 LVCMOS33
led[2] G14 LVCMOS33
led[3] D18 LVCMOS33

# RGB LED LD5
led5_r Y11 LVCMOS33
led5_g T5 LVCMOS33
led5_b Y12 LVCMOS33

# RGB LED LD6
led6_r V16 LVCMOS33
led6_g F17 LVCMOS33
led6_b M17 LVCMOS33
